<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="container container--narrow" data-reveal>
    <h2 class="text-center">About Mike</h2>
    <p class="mt-md">Mike Daws is a passionate arborist with a genuine love for trees. He has a background in tree climbing, previously running a business specialising in tree maintenance, difficult access pruning and habitat creation. A progression to consulting was a natural step, building on the strong familiarity with the physiology and behaviour of trees earned through a career of pruning.</p>
    <p class="mt-md">Mike has a strong eye for assessing tree condition and identifying structural defects. He is an expert in Tree Risk Assessment and holds advanced qualifications under the QTRA framework.</p>
    <p class="mt-md">A background climbing and working in damaged trees has built a strong knowledge base around their behaviour and biomechanics. Mike is uniquely positioned to undertake Level 5 aerial assessments as a climbing consulting arborist.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container container--narrow text-center" data-reveal>
    <h2>Why Qualifications Matter</h2>
    <p class="mt-md">Hiring a qualified arborist means your trees are assessed and managed according to Australian Standards (AS 4373). It also means your arborist reports will be accepted by councils for development applications, insurance claims, and neighbour disputes.</p>
